{"name":"Blue Garter","hex":"#a2b8ce","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"garter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A band worn around the leg to hold up a sock or stocking.","A bendlet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fasten with a garter","To wear a garter"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garter","blocks":[{"text":"A garter is an article of clothing comprising a narrow band of fabric fastened about the leg to keep up stockings. In the 18th to 20th centuries, they were tied just below the knee, where the leg is most slender, to keep the stocking from slipping. The advent of elastic has made them less necessary from this functional standpoint, although they are still often worn for fashion. Garters have been widely worn by men and women, depending on fashion trends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Garter_%28cropped%29.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Garter_%28cropped%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garter","wikidata":"Q13742"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Garter_%28cropped%29.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Garter_%28cropped%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Garter_%28cropped%29.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Garter_%28cropped%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Garter_%28cropped%29.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Garter_%28cropped%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sketch of a garter. The band goes around the leg, and the hook on the lower side attaches to the top of the stocking.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGarter_(cropped).tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mlle._Rhea_Flask_LC-USZ62-99952.jpg/500px-Mlle._Rhea_Flask_LC-USZ62-99952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mlle._Rhea_Flask_LC-USZ62-99952.jpg/500px-Mlle._Rhea_Flask_LC-USZ62-99952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hip flask tucked into a garter during Prohibition","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMlle._Rhea_Flask_LC-USZ62-99952.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Bride_getting_dre